        <h2 id="emerald-conf">emerald.conf</h2>

        <p>
            The file is shell syntax and is sourced by <code>pkgbuild</code>.
            Values can be exported to the build environment or set as
            package-manager policy.
        </p>

        <pre><code>export CFLAGS="-O2 -march=x86-64 -pipe"
export CXXFLAGS="${CFLAGS}"
export FCFLAGS="${CFLAGS}"
export FFLAGS="${CFLAGS}"
export MAKEFLAGS="-j$(nproc)"
export LDFLAGS="-Wl,-O1 -Wl,--as-needed -Wl,-z,pack-relative-relocs"

# SOURCE_DIR="/var/cache/emerald/sources"
# PACKAGE_DIR="/var/cache/emerald/packages"
# WORK_DIR="/var/cache/emerald/work"
# CBUILD_DIR="/var/state/emerald/cbuild"
# CURL_OPTS=""
# COMPRESSION_MODE="xz"
# NO_STRIP="no"
# IGNORE_CHECKSUM="no"
# KEEP_DOC="no"
# KEEP_LIBTOOL="no"
# KEEP_LOCALE="yes"
# KEEP_MAN="yes"
# KEEP_INFO="yes"
# KEEP_HELP="no"
# NOCOLOR="no"
# THEME="vylen"</code></pre>

        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Variable</th>
                    <th>Meaning</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>

            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>CFLAGS</code>, <code>CXXFLAGS</code>,
                        <code>FCFLAGS</code>, <code>FFLAGS</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>
                        Compiler flags inherited by recipes for C, C++, Fortran,
                        and generic Fortran-compatible builds.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>MAKEFLAGS</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>
                        Default parallel make setting.
                        <code>pkgbuild --jobs=N</code> normalizes parallelism
                        for make, Ninja, CMake, Cargo, and Go.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>LDFLAGS</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Linker optimization, as-needed linking, and packed relative relocations.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>SOURCE_DIR</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Downloaded source cache.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>PACKAGE_DIR</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>
                        Completed <code>.epkg.tar.*</code> package cache.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>WORK_DIR</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Per-port unpack and staging workspace.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>CBUILD_DIR</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Saved custom build options and configuration snapshots.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>CURL_OPTS</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Additional curl flags for source downloads.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>COMPRESSION_MODE</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>
                        Package compression: <code>gz</code>, <code>bz2</code>,
                        <code>xz</code>, <code>lz4</code>, or <code>zstd</code>.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>NO_STRIP</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Controls binary stripping during package assembly.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>IGNORE_CHECKSUM</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>
                        Skip checksum verification. Prefer
                        <code>--skip-checksum</code> only for deliberate local debugging.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>KEEP_DOC</code>, <code>KEEP_MAN</code>,
                        <code>KEEP_INFO</code>, <code>KEEP_HELP</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Keep or remove documentation classes during packaging.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>KEEP_LIBTOOL</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Keep libtool artifacts instead of removing them during package cleanup.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>KEEP_LOCALE</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Keep locale data when pruning package contents.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>NOCOLOR</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Disable colored status output.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <code>THEME</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>
                        Status theme; the source documents <code>dracula</code>,
                        <code>nord</code>, and <code>vylen</code>.
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 id="repo">emerald.repo</h2>

        <p>
            Each active line has three fields: local checkout directory,
            repository URL, and optional branch. The default branch is
            <code>main</code>.
        </p>

        <pre><code>/usr/ports/core https://gitlab.com/vylen/ports/core
#/usr/ports/extra https://gitlab.com/vylen/ports/extra
#/usr/ports/community https://gitlab.com/vylen/ports/community</code></pre>

        <p>
            Uncomment optional repositories only after reviewing their trust and
            port policy. Use <code>--repo-file</code>,
            <code>--append-repo</code>, <code>--prepend-repo</code>, or
            <code>--override-repo</code> for one-off changes.
        </p>

        <h2 id="alias">emerald.alias</h2>

        <p>
            One mapping per line: the real package followed by its aliased
            package. Comments and blank lines are ignored.
        </p>

        <pre><code># real-package aliased-package
openssl libressl</code></pre>

        <p>
            This supports dependency compatibility. Manage it through
            <code>emerald alias list|add|remove</code> rather than editing
            blindly.
        </p>

        <h2 id="mask">emerald.mask</h2>

        <p>
            One port name per line. A masked port remains installed but is
            excluded from <code>emerald sysup</code>.
        </p>

        <pre><code># hold this package during a planned migration
openssl</code></pre>

        <p>
            Use <code>emerald mask add</code> and
            <code>emerald mask remove</code>, and document why every long-lived
            mask exists.
        </p>

        <h2 id="revdep">revdep.conf</h2>

        <p>
            The reverse-dependency scanner accepts three exclusion classes.
            Directories must be absolute and end with <code>/</code>. Files must
            be absolute paths. Libraries are names; binaries depending on an
            excluded library are ignored.
        </p>

        <pre><code># directories
/usr/local/

# files
/usr/lib/example/libcompat.so

# library names
libvendor-private.so</code></pre>

        <p>
            Additional files can be placed in <code>/etc/revdep.d/*.conf</code>.
            Exclude only known intentional exceptions; broad exclusions reduce
            the value of the audit.
        </p>
